load @/code/octonion
  find octonion

load @/code/algebra/cayley-dickson
  find cayley-dickson-double

note <The sedenions, the Cayley-Dickson double of the octonions, dimension sixteen. They are the cliff. Because the octonions are not associative, doubling them loses the norm, so the sedenions are not a composition algebra and they have zero divisors, two nonzero sedenions whose product is zero. So reversibility fails here, which is why the reversible tower stops one rung below, at the octonions. This is the lower wall the pinch-point sits just above.>

form sedenion
  link source, like cayley-dickson-double
  link base, like octonion
